From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:54:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs: record patches 179 to 193 in the stack manifest

Phase P5 of the IndexedDB redesign, the connection lifecycle: a worker's
IndexedDB teardown when its event loop ends (179), the connection queue
per database with versionchange, blocked and close pending, and the spec
deleteDatabase (180), the storage proxy map obtained in parallel (181),
the owner's wake-up of a terminated idle dedicated worker (182), a shared
worker closed once its last owner document is gone (183), a page in the
back/forward cache evicted when its connection gets a versionchange event
(184), the forced close of the connections to an unusable database
(185), the client storage registry's lookup and list of a bottle's
databases (186), the manager's client storage calls on a thread of their
own instead of the global pool (187), databases of earlier sessions found
in the registry for open, deleteDatabase and databases() (188), a
request's backend failure reported with its own error instead of a
DataError (189), a cached page evicted when it holds back another page's
request or transaction, and blocked fired for connections that were
already closing (190), the connections of windows whose event loop died
closed when the constellation reports them (191), and corrupt databases
reset when they are opened, the owner's decision (192).

The fixes of the P5 review are folded into 179, 180 and 183 to 189;
190 to 192 are new. 187's watch is the client storage handle now, whose
calls the thread makes, rather than the thread pool.

182 is a cherry-pick (`git cherry-pick -x`) of the owner's commit
f2e87c24b04 from the branch servo-leaks-worker-terminate, which isn't
upstream yet; its message keeps the original text and adds the fork part
after a `----` line. Drop it once the commit lands upstream, but keep its
expectation change.

All of 179 to 192 change upstream files (script, constellation,
shared/storage, the storage component, WPT metadata), so they are tier C;
this bookkeeping entry is B, like the earlier ones.

Validation: `uv run docs/ohos-sync/check_stack.py base/2026-11-09` passes.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written by the agent, with the patches generated by gen_patches.py)
